{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/647228-was-hoping-we-d-get-this","id":647228,"title":"Was hoping we'd get this!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-31T14:44:04-07:00","id":647228,"title":"Was hoping we'd get this!","content":"So ever since I bothered to read some of the Pugmire stuff, I became interested, but couldn't find a place to discuss it. So I'm glad we finally have a forum to do so.<br /> <br /> In one of the articles, they discussed possible additional races to the game, one of which being birds. Personally, I think Birds would make wonderful enemies to the Dogs, serving as advent opposition to humanity's legacy.<br /> <br /> I mean it makes sense after all. Dogs used to live in luxury, but what did birds get? Their wings were clipped, they were locked in cages all day, left to shit on the floor, and often having little to eat besides water and salted bread. It sounds like the birds would be glad humanity was gone and hate the dogs for revering them as some great beings. What could be even more devious is if their evolution stripped them of their ability to fly (gliding, perhaps) and they blame it on humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-31-2015, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T04:19:14-07:00","id":648732,"title":"","content":"Not to mention bird-hunting dog breeds, like retrievers. There might even be a bit of rivalry between birds whose ancestors were trained for hunting (falc